.TH MXTOP 1 "2026-07" "metax-mxtop" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mxtop \- an nvitop-like interactive terminal monitor for MetaX GPUs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mxtop
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B mxtop
.B \-\-once
|
.B \-\-json
.RB [ \-\-count
.IR N ]
.br
.B mxtop
.B \-\-remote\-mode
.RB [ \-\-nodes
.IR HOST .\|.\|.]
.RB [ \-\-auth\-token
.IR TOKEN ]
.RB [ \-\-tls\-cert
.I CERTFILE
.B \-\-tls\-key
.IR KEYFILE ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mxtop
displays live telemetry for MetaX GPUs: per-device temperature, power,
utilization, memory, memory bandwidth, and clocks; host CPU/memory/swap
history graphs; and a sortable, filterable GPU process table with
per-process metrics, environment, and tree views.
.PP
Telemetry is read-only through MXSML/Pymxsml or the
.B mx-smi
CLI.
.B mxtop
never updates firmware, resets GPUs, or changes persistence or
administration settings. Process signals (SIGINT, SIGTERM, SIGKILL) are
presented for confirmation, validate process identity against PID reuse,
and require process ownership unless run as root; use
.B \-\-readonly
to disable them entirely.
.SH MODES
The default mode runs the interactive monitor when stdin and stdout are
terminals, and prints one snapshot otherwise.
.TP
.BR \-\-monitor ", " \-m " [" auto | full | compact ]
Run interactively with the given layout.
.TP
.BR \-\-once ", " \-1
Print one ANSI-colored text snapshot and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print one machine-readable JSON snapshot and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-json\-lines ", " \-\-ndjson
Print snapshots as one compact JSON object per line (NDJSON), for
streaming pipelines. Combines with
.BR \-\-count .
.TP
.BR \-\-count ", " \-n " " \fIN\fR
With
.B \-\-once
or
.BR \-\-json ,
print
.I N
snapshots separated by
.B \-\-interval
seconds. Implies
.B \-\-once
when neither is given.
.TP
.B \-\-remote\-mode
Serve a local web dashboard aggregating multiple SSH-reachable nodes.
See
.B REMOTE MODE
below.
.TP
.B \-\-export\-metrics
Serve this host's telemetry as a Prometheus
.I /metrics
endpoint (default port 9532) without SSH. Honors
.BR \-\-bind ,
.BR \-\-port ,
.BR \-\-auth\-token ,
the direct TLS options,
and samples at
.BR \-\-interval .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-version ", " \-V
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-print\-completion \fR{bash,zsh,fish}
Print a shell completion script on stdout and exit. For example:
.B mxtop \-\-print\-completion bash > /etc/bash_completion.d/mxtop
.TP
.B \-\-doctor
Diagnose the environment and exit: backend availability (Pymxsml, mx-smi),
device visibility, psutil, terminal capabilities, config file validity, and
the remote extra. Prints PASS/WARN/FAIL per check with fix hints; exits
non-zero when no telemetry backend works.
.TP
.B \-\-backend \fR{auto,pymxsml,mxsmi}
Select the telemetry backend (default: auto, preferring Pymxsml).
.TP
.B \-\-interval \fISEC\fR
Refresh interval in seconds (default: 2.0, minimum 0.25).
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-unicode ", " \-\-ascii ", " \-U
Use ASCII characters only. Automatic for non-UTF-8 locales.
.TP
.B \-\-readonly
Disable process-changing actions in the interactive UI.
.SS Coloring
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable ANSI colors.
.TP
.B \-\-colorful
Spectrum-like gradient bar colors (requires 256-color terminal support).
.TP
.B \-\-light
Colors suitable for light terminal themes.
.TP
.B \-\-force\-color
Emit ANSI color even when stdout is not a TTY.
.TP
.B \-\-gpu\-util\-thresh \fILOW HIGH\fR
GPU utilization intensity thresholds (default: 10 75).
.TP
.B \-\-mem\-util\-thresh \fILOW HIGH\fR
GPU memory intensity thresholds (default: 10 80).
.SS Device and process filtering
.TP
.BR \-\-only ", " \-o " " \fIINDEX\fR.\|.\|.
Show only the selected GPU indices.
.TP
.BR \-\-only\-visible ", " \-ov
Follow MACA_VISIBLE_DEVICES or CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES.
.TP
.BR \-\-compute ", " \-c " / " \-\-only\-compute ", " \-C
Show processes with a compute context / exactly compute-only processes.
.TP
.BR \-\-graphics ", " \-g " / " \-\-only\-graphics ", " \-G
Show processes with a graphics context / exactly graphics-only processes.
.TP
.BR \-\-user ", " \-u " [" \fIUSERNAME\fR.\|.\|.]
Show selected users (the current user when the list is empty).
.TP
.BR \-\-pid ", " \-p " " \fIPID\fR.\|.\|.
Show only the selected process IDs.
.SH REMOTE MODE
.B mxtop \-\-remote\-mode
opens persistent SSH connections (key/agent authentication only) to the
nodes given by
.B \-\-nodes
or
.BR \-\-nodes\-file ,
or auto-discovered from
.I ~/.ssh/config
when neither is given (or with
.BR \-\-discover ).
It serves a live web dashboard with a fleet overview, GPU heatmap, trend
sparklines, node inventory, process table, and per-node detail.
.TP
.B \-\-port \fIPORT\fR
Dashboard port (default: 8080), or exporter port (default: 9532).
.TP
.B \-\-bind \fIADDR\fR
Bind address (default: 127.0.0.1). Binding beyond localhost prints a transport
warning without TLS and a separate access warning without
.BR \-\-auth\-token .
.TP
.B \-\-auth\-token \fITOKEN\fR
Require this shared token for dashboard or exporter access. API and Prometheus
clients use
.B Authorization: Bearer
while a browser can make a one-time
.B ?token=
visit that sets an HttpOnly cookie. Defaults to the
.B MXTOP_AUTH_TOKEN
environment variable.
.TP
.B \-\-tls\-cert \fICERTFILE\fR
PEM certificate chain for direct HTTPS. The file must contain the server
certificate followed by any intermediate certificates. Requires
.BR \-\-tls\-key .
Supported by both
.B \-\-remote\-mode
and
.BR \-\-export\-metrics .
.TP
.B \-\-tls\-key \fIKEYFILE\fR
PEM private key matching
.BR \-\-tls\-cert .
The certificate and key options must be supplied together.
.TP
.B \-\-tls\-key\-password\-file \fIFILE\fR
Read an encrypted TLS private key's password from one non-empty line in
.IR FILE .
Requires both certificate and key options. Protect this file and the private
key so only the mxtop service account can read them.
.PP
The certificate Subject Alternative Name must cover every hostname or IP
address used by browsers and scrapers. A wildcard bind is advertised locally as
.BR localhost ;
include that name in the SAN for
.B \-\-open
or open the certificate's actual DNS name manually. Install a self-signed or private CA in
each client trust store; for Prometheus, set
.B scheme: https
and
.B tls_config.ca_file
instead of disabling verification. TLS encrypts traffic but does not replace
.BR \-\-auth\-token ,
firewall rules, a narrow bind address, or an HTTPS reverse proxy where one is
operationally appropriate. TLS files are loaded once; restart mxtop after
certificate renewal, key rotation, or password-file changes.
.TP
.B \-\-remote\-mxsmi\-path \fIPATH\fR
Path to mx-smi on the remote hosts.
.TP
.B \-\-remote\-command\-timeout \fISEC\fR
Maximum time for each remote telemetry command (default: 10 seconds,
minimum: 0.1). A timed-out command marks that node down for the sample and
reconnects it on the next poll instead of blocking the whole cluster.
.TP
.B \-\-open
Open the dashboard in a browser.
.SH INTERACTIVE KEYS
.TP
.B a f c
Switch to auto, full, or compact layout.
.TP
.B h ?
Help screen.
.TP
.B F5 r
Refresh immediately and resume if paused.
.TP
.B p Z
Pause or resume live updates on the main screen.
.TP
.B Arrows, Tab/Shift-Tab, Home, End
Move the process selection.
.TP
.B Space
Tag/untag the current process; tagged processes form the signal target set.
.TP
.B \\\\ F4
Incremental filter: typed text matches user, command, or PID;
Enter applies, Esc clears.
.TP
.B Esc
Clear the filter first, then selection and tags.
.TP
.B , . / o\fIkey\fR
Cycle sort column / invert order / direct sort
.RB ( n
GPU,
.B p
PID,
.B u
USER,
.B g
GPU-MEM,
.B s
%SM,
.B b
%GMBW,
.B c
%CPU,
.B m
%MEM,
.B t
TIME; uppercase reverses). Column headers are also click-to-sort.
.TP
.B e t Enter
Process environment / tree view / metrics screen.
.TP
.B Ctrl-C I K T
Send SIGINT / SIGINT / SIGKILL / SIGTERM to the selected or tagged
processes (with confirmation).
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Persistent defaults are read from
.IR ~/.config/mxtop/config.toml ,
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/mxtop/config.toml ,
or the file named by
.BR MXTOP_CONFIG .
CLI flags and environment variables take precedence. Keys:
.BR interval ,
.BR monitor ,
.BR colorful ,
.BR light ,
.BR readonly ,
.BR no-unicode ,
.BR gpu-util-thresh ,
.BR mem-util-thresh ,
and a
.B [remote]
table with
.BR bind ,
.BR port ,
.BR auth-token ,
.BR tls-cert ,
.BR tls-key ,
.BR tls-key-password-file ,
.BR mxsmi-path ,
.BR command-timeout ,
.BR open .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MXTOP_MXSMI_PATH
Path to the local mx-smi executable.
.TP
.B MXTOP_MONITOR_MODE
Comma-separated defaults: auto|full|compact, colorful|plain, light|dark,
readonly.
.TP
.B MXTOP_GPU_UTILIZATION_THRESHOLDS, MXTOP_MEMORY_UTILIZATION_THRESHOLDS
LOW,HIGH intensity thresholds.
.TP
.B MXTOP_AUTH_TOKEN
Default access token for \-\-remote\-mode or \-\-export\-metrics.
.TP
.B MXTOP_CONFIG
Path to the configuration file.
.TP
.B MACA_VISIBLE_DEVICES, CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES
Device visibility lists for \-\-only\-visible.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR, ANSI_COLORS_DISABLED, FORCE_COLOR
Standard color overrides.
.TP
.B MXTOP_PYMXSML_ECC_ERRORS
Set to 1/true/yes/on to opt into cached ECC-error polling.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 on backend or telemetry errors (invalid device indices in
one-shot output also yield 1); 2 on usage errors.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Interactive full layout, 1s refresh:
.B mxtop \-m full \-\-interval 1
.TP
Ten text snapshots five seconds apart:
.B mxtop \-n 10 \-\-interval 5
.TP
One minute of JSON samples for logging:
.B mxtop \-\-json \-n 60 \-\-interval 1
.TP
Cluster dashboard for three nodes with a token:
.B mxtop \-\-remote\-mode \-\-nodes nodeA nodeB nodeC \-\-auth\-token secret \-\-open
.TP
Direct-HTTPS exporter with a matching certificate and private key:
.B mxtop \-\-export\-metrics \-\-bind 0.0.0.0 \-\-tls\-cert /etc/mxtop/fullchain.pem \-\-tls\-key /etc/mxtop/privkey.pem
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mx-smi (1),
.BR top (1),
.BR htop (1)
.PP
